Every listed direct-SQL writer exists on the CRM connection (PSQL/ALTSHULER_MSCRM). The Execute SQL tasks have no configuration override. The writers are:
- update Contact;
- insert gen_contactlinkBase;
- update gen_contactlink, with the object type correctly hedged as a CRM convention;
- insert and update gen_instructionprovisionBase;
- update gen_customeraccountbase (risk) and Gen_customeraccountBase (employee mobile phone);
- insert gen_warningnotetypebase;
- insert and update gen_warningnotebase;
- update ContactBase twice.

The four Execute SQL statements are quoted exactly. The only SDK writers outside ETL plumbing are gen_beneficiaries Delete/Create/Update and contact Create.
